namespace jobs.deliver;

import app;
import db.work;

--- Five attempts, thirty seconds apart, then `public._jwc_jobs_dead`.
---
--- The handler runs on a worker, minutes after whatever dispatched it, so
--- it has its parameters and the database and nothing else: no request, no
--- response, no `context`.
---
--- It also has to tolerate running twice. A worker that dies mid-job loses
--- its lease and the job is redelivered — that is the at-least-once
--- guarantee, and it is the strongest one a queue on a database can make.
job Deliver(recipient: text, subject: text) retries 5 backoff "30s" {
    insert into App.work.Deliveries { recipient = $recipient, subject = $subject };
}
